{"availability":"available","full":"pittner/free-habit-tracker-no-streak-guilt","name":"free-habit-tracker-no-streak-guilt","description":"Free browser habit tracker that forgives missed days — no streak resets to zero, no guilt, ADHD-friendly. No signup, 100% private. A free tool by BeMooore.","category":"Productivity","language":"HTML","stars":0,"forks":0,"created":"2026-08-14T07:31:25Z","updated":"2026-08-18T02:20:19Z","license":"MIT","branch":"main","homepage":"https://pittner.github.io/free-habit-tracker-no-streak-guilt/","topics":["adhd","free-tool","github-pages","habit-tracker","javascript","no-signup","privacy","productivity","self-improvement","streak"],"demo":"https://pittner.github.io/free-habit-tracker-no-streak-guilt/","color":"#63362a","ink":"#f8c7a8","lastCheckedAt":"2026-10-08T20:10:54.797Z","lastAttemptAt":"2026-10-08T20:10:54.797Z","lastAvailableAt":"2026-10-08T20:10:54.797Z","metrics":[{"at":"2026-10-08T20:10:54.797Z","stars":0,"forks":0}],"technologies":[],"overview":{"kind":"readme","version":1,"paragraphs":["A free, private, no-signup habit tracker that forgives your missed days. One bad day never resets your progress to zero, there's no red X of shame, and it's built for brains that don't run on perfect chains (hi, ADHD). Everything is stored locally in your browser — nothing is ever uploaded.","Most habit apps are built on punishment: string together a streak, miss one day, watch the counter reset to 0 in red, then avoid the app out of guilt. That's not a willpower problem — it's a design problem. The missed day is the most useful moment there is (it tells you what gets in your way), so this tool keeps your progress visible after a slip and makes coming back feel easy instead of shameful."],"features":[],"sourceUrl":"https://github.com/pittner/free-habit-tracker-no-streak-guilt/blob/main/README.md","fingerprint":"1ab26bdafeab35bcd73165bef4316f78dbbe4663bc7e3f3110c2e6ce19e61e56","extractedAt":"2026-10-08T20:10:54.912Z"},"overviewCheckedAt":"2